OpenWings patch 0024: OpenWings wording (no upstream name or sea words)

People should never meet the upstream name or its nautical wording. This
patch replaces what they can see or receive, and what the model is told
about itself, with plain OpenWings wording. Identifiers and anything other
software reads stay as they are.

  * Text in the app: chat headers after a delete, the Deep Research
    placeholder, calendar quick-add examples (no Ithaca or Penelope), the
    /demo and window tours, Cookbook text and its [openwings] log tags, the
    reminder clean-up button, the theme colour label, less common messages
    and tooltips, the companion pairing page, the desktop launcher's splash
    and tray. The hidden /odyssey easter egg is removed.
  * The built-in persona "Odysseus, king of Ithaca" is a neutral
    Strategist (static/js/presets.js, src/reminder_personas.py,
    static/js/tasks.js). Its id 'odysseus' is kept, so saved reminder, task
    and group choices keep working; a chat or hidden-persona entry saved
    under the old name still resolves and is moved to the new name, and
    src/preset_manager.py moves an active custom slot that still holds the
    old built-in persona to the new name and prompt.
  * What the model reads: identity prompts ("You are the OpenWings
    assistant."), system-prompt rules and tool descriptions
    (src/agent_loop.py, src/tool_schemas.py, src/tool_index.py,
    mcp_servers/email_server.py and others) no longer name Odysseus. The
    short prompts that go only to upstream's own fine-tuned odysseus-*
    models (the minimal document, notes and general paths and the Qwen
    router prompts in src/agent_loop.py) keep the wording those models
    were trained on; people only meet them when they run such a model,
    whose name already says Odysseus.
    Phrases people type that name the app ("my openwings settings",
    "connected to OpenWings") are recognised next to the old ones.
  * What people receive: reminder mail subject "Reminder (OpenWings): ..."
    (the old subject is still matched by the Reminders filter, Clear and
    the urgent-mail scanner), urgent-mail alert links, push and Discord
    test messages, webhook test pings, calendar PRODIDs, the two-factor
    issuer for new enrolments, research report labels, the search results
    title, User-Agents, OpenRouter attribution, and the API docs title.
  * Downloads: openwings_backup_<timestamp>.json, openwings-contacts.csv
    and .vcf, openwings_<theme>.json (restore and import read the content,
    not the name).
  * static/wave-variants.html, whirlpool-variants.html,
    modal-control-variants.html, research-ascii-variants.html (and its .js):
    upstream design test pages, served to anyone, are deleted (the image
    build removes them, overlay/UPSTREAM_DELETED).
  * setup.py: the container log banner says OpenWings.
  * Names that did not match: the sidebar's Agents opens a window titled
    Agents (static/js/wings-ui.js; the composer's Prompt item still opens
    it as Prompt); Settings and the dock call Files & Docs by that name,
    not Library; scheduled tasks read "Every 5 new chats", not "Every 5
    session createds" (static/js/tasks.js, whose "waiting until idle"
    checks also match the new queued text); the Skills badge counts
    built-in skills; the composer keeps "Message OpenWings..." on touch
    screens (static/app.js no longer swaps in a swipe hint every 5s);
    /theme and /setup theme take and list the names people see ("Lichen",
    "Duet night"), not the theme keys (static/js/slashCommands.js).
  * Upstream traces: the login page shows the OpenWings version, not
    upstream's build number; Settings shows integration keys masked
    (••••EPYz), without the keys' internal prefix; /favicon.ico is the
    OpenWings icon (app.py, before sign-in too); a browser that opens an
    address that does not exist gets an OpenWings page in the user's look
    (app.py, wings/pages.py), while API routes and non-HTML clients keep
    the JSON answer.
  * Unchanged on purpose: X-Odysseus-* mail headers and webhook header
    names, odysseus:// attachment references, Copilot headers, the
    companion's server name, ODYSSEUS_* settings, API paths, storage keys,
    and the stored incognito session name 'Nobody' (upstream's tidy
    deletes sessions named 'Incognito'; the label people see already says
    Incognito, patch 0020).
  * tests/: upstream tests that assert the old wording follow it (tests
    are not part of the image).

Applies to: odysseus-dev/odysseus@9d0d3720f4ca181d87bef94da826d730acc6d483
